BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Jacobs School of Music
DTSTART:20260709T230000Z
DTEND:20260710T010000Z
LOCATION:Sweeney Hall
GEO:39.165773;-86.517674
SUMMARY:Guest Lecture – An Encounter with Violinist William Harvey
DESCRIPTION:About the Artist  Concertmaster of Mexico's premier orchestra
 \, the Orquesta Sinfónica Nacional\, and violin faculty at the Universid
 ad Panamericana\, violinist\, conductor\, and composer William Harvey has
  appeared as violin soloist at Carnegie Hall with the New York Youth Symp
 hony and has performed concerti with orchestras in Argentina\, El Salvado
 r\, the Philippines\, Mexico\, and the United States. His recording of th
 e violin concerto by Hector Infanzón garnered two nominations to the Lat
 in Grammys in 2021. For four years\, he served as the violin and viola te
 acher at Afghanistan National Institute of Music (ANIM)\, founding the Af
 ghan Youth Orchestra (AYO)\, which he conducted for President Hamid Karza
 i and led on a historic tour of the United States in concerts at Carnegie
  Hall and the Kennedy Center. Harvey also conducted AYO on the 2012 and 2
 013 season finales of Afghan Star. He also published anthologies of Afgha
 n songs arranged for strings. He has previously served as concertmaster o
 f the Orquesta Sinfónica Sinaloa Las Artes (Mexico)\, Orquesta Sinfónic
 a de la Universidad Nacional de San Juan (Argentina) and the Spokane Symp
 hony\, faculty at Indiana University's Summer String Academy\, fellow at 
 Carnegie Hall's Academy\, and guest artist at the Myanmar Music Festival\
 , Mehli Mehta Music Foundation\, and Iguazu en Concierto. He has performe
 d at festivals throughout Mexico\, including the Festival del Centro Hist
 órico. As a conductor\, he has led professional orchestras throughout Me
 xico and youth orchestras in Argentina\, Qatar\, the Philippines\, Zimbab
 we\, and the United States. Harvey's compositions have received over a hu
 ndred performances. Harvey earned his M.M. from The Juilliard School\, wh
 ere he studied violin with Ronald Copes and composition with Samuel Adler
 \, and B.M. from the IU Jacobs School of Music\, where he studied violin 
 with Mimi Zweig and composition with Sven-David Sandström. In 2005\, Har
 vey founded Cultures in Harmony. CiH workshops in Pakistan\, Qatar\, Egyp
 t\, the Philippines\, Tunisia\, Zimbabwe\, and Mexico have benefited thou
 sands of young musicians. Harvey plays on violins made by Joseph Curtin (
 2001) and Nadia Sánchez (2021).
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>About the Artist</strong><br /><b
 r />  Concertmaster of Mexico's premier orchestra\, the Orquesta Sinfóni
 ca Nacional\, and violin faculty at the Universidad Panamericana\, violin
 ist\, conductor\, and composer <strong>William Harvey</strong> has appear
 ed as violin soloist at Carnegie Hall with the New York Youth Symphony an
 d has performed concerti with orchestras in Argentina\, El Salvador\, the
  Philippines\, Mexico\, and the United States. His recording of the violi
 n concerto by Hector Infanzón garnered two nominations to the Latin Gram
 mys in 2021. For four years\, he served as the violin and viola teacher a
 t Afghanistan National Institute of Music (ANIM)\, founding the Afghan Yo
 uth Orchestra (AYO)\, which he conducted for President Hamid Karzai and l
 ed on a historic tour of the United States in concerts at Carnegie Hall a
 nd the Kennedy Center. Harvey also conducted AYO on the 2012 and 2013 sea
 son finales of <em>Afghan Star</em>. He also published anthologies of Afg
 han songs arranged for strings. He has previously served as concertmaster
  of the Orquesta Sinfónica Sinaloa Las Artes (Mexico)\, Orquesta Sinfón
 ica de la Universidad Nacional de San Juan (Argentina) and the Spokane Sy
 mphony\, faculty at Indiana University's Summer String Academy\, fellow a
 t Carnegie Hall's Academy\, and guest artist at the Myanmar Music Festiva
 l\, Mehli Mehta Music Foundation\, and Iguazu en Concierto. He has perfor
 med at festivals throughout Mexico\, including the Festival del Centro Hi
 stórico. As a conductor\, he has led professional orchestras throughout 
 Mexico and youth orchestras in Argentina\, Qatar\, the Philippines\, Zimb
 abwe\, and the United States. Harvey's compositions have received over a 
 hundred performances. Harvey earned his M.M. from The Juilliard School\, 
 where he studied violin with Ronald Copes and composition with Samuel Adl
 er\, and B.M. from the IU Jacobs School of Music\, where he studied violi
 n with Mimi Zweig and composition with Sven-David Sandström. In 2005\, H
 arvey founded Cultures in Harmony. CiH workshops in Pakistan\, Qatar\, Eg
 ypt\, the Philippines\, Tunisia\, Zimbabwe\, and Mexico have benefited th
 ousands of young musicians. Harvey plays on violins made by Joseph Curtin
  (2001) and Nadia Sánchez (2021).</p>
